><meta name="description" content="On July 8, 2026, OpenAI replaced Advanced Voice Mode with GPT-Live, a full-duplex voice that listens and speaks at the same time. Here is what changed, how…"/><link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.json"/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.voiceos.com/blog/gpt-live-full-duplex-voice"/><link rel="alternate" hrefLang="en" href="https://www.voiceos.com/blog/gpt-live-full-duplex-voice"/><link rel="alternate" hrefLang="ja" href="https://www.voiceos.com/ja/blog/gpt-live-full-duplex-voice"/><link rel="alternate" hrefLang="x-default" href="https://www.voiceos.com/blog/gpt-live-full-duplex-voice"/><meta name="google-site-verification" content="uFUtX2rdWjK_rXafEbA9qRvv_m7amTpZJMnUywraMXg"/><meta property="og:title" content="GPT-Live Is Here: ChatGPT&#x27;s Voice Now Listens and Talks at Once, Just Like &#x27;Her&#x27; and JARVIS"/><meta property="og:description" content="On July 8, 2026, OpenAI replaced Advanced Voice Mode with GPT-Live, a full-duplex voice that listens and speaks at the same time. Here is what changed, how full-duplex differs from the old turn-based voice, and why it means voice is becoming the operating system for real work."/><meta property="og:url" content="https://www.voiceos.com/blog/gpt-live-full-duplex-voice"/><meta property="og:image" content="https://www.voiceos.com/blogs/gpt-live-full-duplex-voice.png"/><meta property="og:image:width" content="1200"/><meta property="og:image:height" content="630"/><meta property="og:type" content="article"/><meta property="article:published_time" content="2026-07-09T08:00:00.000Z"/><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"/><meta name="twitter:title" content="GPT-Live Is Here: ChatGPT&#x27;s Voice Now Listens and Talks at Once, Just Like &#x27;Her&#x27; and JARVIS"/><meta name="twitter:description" content="On July 8, 2026, OpenAI replaced Advanced Voice Mode with GPT-Live, a full-duplex voice that listens and speaks at the same time. Here is what changed, how full-duplex differs from the old turn-based voice, and why it means voice is becoming the operating system for real work."/><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://www.voiceos.com/blogs/gpt-live-full-duplex-voice.png"/><link rel="shortcut icon" href="/favicon.ico"/><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="16x16 32x32 48x48 64x64 128x128 256x256" type="image/x-icon"/><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png" sizes="96x96" type="image/png"/><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" sizes="180x180" type="image/png"/><meta name="next-size-adjust" content=""/><link rel="alternate" type="text/plain" href="/llms.txt" title="LLM-readable site description"/><link rel="describedby" type="text/plain" href="/llms-full.txt" title="Full LLM-readable VoiceOS documentation"/><link rel="alternate" type="text/markdown" href="/agents.md" title="VoiceOS agent instructions"/><link rel="alternate" type="text/markdown" href="/pricing.md" title="VoiceOS machine-readable pricing"/><link rel="alternate" type="text/markdown" href="/index.md" title="VoiceOS markdown homepage"/><link rel="alternate" type="application/json" href="/.well-known/agent-card.json" title="VoiceOS agent card"/><link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" href="/rss.xml" title="VoiceOS Blog RSS Feed"/><link rel="preload" as="image" href="/skyCloudsHero-mobile.webp" media="(max-width: 767px)" fetchPriority="high"/><link rel="preload" as="image" href="/skyCloudsHero.webp" media="(min-width: 768px)" fetchPriority="high"/><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Organization","@id":"https://www.voiceos.com/#organization","name":"WakoAI Inc.","legalName":"WakoAI Inc.","alternateName":"VoiceOS","url":"https://www.voiceos.com","email":"support@voiceos.com","description":"WakoAI Inc. builds VoiceOS, an AI voice agent and system-wide dictation app for Mac and Windows.","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.voiceos.com/voiceOsLogo.png"},"brand":{"@type":"Brand","name":"VoiceOS","url":"https://www.voiceos.com"},"founder":[{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.voiceos.com/authors/jonah-daian#person","name":"Jonah Daian","url":"https://www.voiceos.com/authors/jonah-daian"},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://www.voiceos.com/authors/kai-brokering#person","name":"Kai Brokering","url":"https://www.voiceos.com/authors/kai-brokering"}],"sameAs":["https://www.linkedin.com/company/voice-os/","https://x.com/VoiceOSApp","https://www.producthunt.com/products/voiceos","https://www.ycombinator.com/launches/PP3-voiceos-the-siri-for-productivity","https://docs.voiceos.com/"],"knowsAbout":["AI dictation","voice agents","desktop productivity","voice-to-action workflows","hands-free computing","workflow automation"],"contactPoint":[{"@type":"ContactPoint","contactType":"customer support","email":"support@voiceos.com","availableLanguage":["English","Japanese"]}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://www.voiceos.com/#website","url":"https://www.voiceos.com","name":"VoiceOS","description":"VoiceOS is a voice operating system that turns voice to action. The AI voice assistant for Mac and Windows: dictate, send messages, search the web, and automate apps by voice. Try it free.","inLanguage":["en","ja"],"publisher":{"@id":"https://www.voiceos.com/#organization"}}</script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/0cz1d0mv5g_q7.js" noModule=""></script></head><body><div hidden=""><!--$--><!--/$--></div><!--$--><!--/$--><!--$--><!--/$--><!--$--><!--/$--><main class="min-h-screen" style="background-color:#F9F9F9"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"GPT-Live Is Here: ChatGPT's Voice Now Listens and Talks at Once, Just Like 'Her' and JARVIS","description":"On July 8, 2026, OpenAI replaced Advanced Voice Mode with GPT-Live, a full-duplex voice that listens and speaks at the same time. Here is what changed, how full-duplex differs from the old turn-based voice, and why it means voice is becoming the operating system for real work.","image":"https://www.voiceos.com/blogs/gpt-live-full-duplex-voice.png","datePublished":"2026-07-09T08:00:00.000Z","dateModified":"2026-07-09T08:00:00.000Z","inLanguage":"en","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Kai Brokering","@id":"https://www.voiceos.com/authors/kai-brokering#person","url":"https://www.voiceos.com/authors/kai-brokering"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"WakoAI Inc.","url":"https://www.voiceos.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.voiceos.com/voiceOsLogo.png"}},"mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.voiceos.com/blog/gpt-live-full-duplex-voice"},"breadcrumb":{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.voiceos.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Blog","item":"https://www.voiceos.com/blog"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"GPT-Live Is Here: ChatGPT's Voice Now Listens and Talks at Once, Just Like 'Her' and JARVIS","item":"https://www.voiceos.com/blog/gpt-live-full-duplex-voice"}]}}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is GPT-Live?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"GPT-Live is OpenAI's new generation of ChatGPT Voice, launched on July 8, 2026. It is a full-duplex voice model, meaning it can listen and speak at the same time, which makes talking to ChatGPT feel much more like a real conversation. It comes in two versions, GPT-Live-1 and GPT-Live-1 mini, and replaces the older Advanced Voice Mode."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When was GPT-Live released and where can I use it?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"OpenAI released GPT-Live on July 8, 2026. It is rolling out globally inside the ChatGPT app on iOS and Android and on ChatGPT.com on the web, where it becomes the default voice experience. OpenAI said support in the API is coming soon."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is GPT-Live different from Advanced Voice Mode?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Advanced Voice Mode was half-duplex: it chained a speech-to-text model, a language model, and a text-to-speech model, which forced strict turn-taking. GPT-Live is full-duplex, a single model that listens and speaks simultaneously, adds natural cues like \"mhmm\" and \"yeah,\" handles interruptions gracefully, and hands hard questions to a stronger model (GPT-5.5 at launch) in the background. In OpenAI's testing, people preferred GPT-Live 75.7% of the time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which ChatGPT plans get GPT-Live-1 versus GPT-Live-1 mini?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"GPT-Live-1 is the default voice model for paid subscribers on the Go, Plus, and Pro plans. GPT-Live-1 mini is the default for free users. Both replace Advanced Voice Mode as the standard ChatGPT Voice experience."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is ChatGPT's new voice like the movie Her?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"That is the comparison many people reach for. Like the AI in the 2013 film Her, GPT-Live holds a flowing, natural conversation, listens while it talks, and responds without the awkward pauses of older assistants. OpenAI has drawn Her comparisons before, including the Sky voice it pulled in 2024. GPT-Live is the closest a mainstream product has come to that experience."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does this mean I can have a real-life JARVIS?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A natural voice like GPT-Live is one half of the JARVIS idea. The other half is a computer that can actually take action across your apps, not just talk. For that you need a system-wide voice layer. VoiceOS brings a JARVIS-style assistant to Mac and Windows: you talk, and it dictates, edits, answers questions about your screen, and takes actions across apps like Gmail, Slack, and Calendar."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is voice really becoming the new operating system?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The direction is clear. OpenAI's own ChatGPT Voice lead described voice as becoming \"a kind of primary interface to computing.\" As AI learns to understand intent rather than fixed commands, talking becomes a primary way to operate a computer, alongside the keyboard and mouse. Tools like VoiceOS take that further by letting your voice act across every app on your desktop, not just inside one chatbot."}}]}</script><nav data-scrolled="false" class="nav-root fixed left-0 right-0 z-50" style="top:0;--nav-notch-clip:polygon(0.000px 0.000px, calc(100% - 0.000px) 0.000px, calc(100% - 1.929px) 0.117px, calc(100% - 3.829px) 0.465px, calc(100% - 5.674px) 1.040px, calc(100% - 7.436px) 1.833px, calc(100% - 9.089px) 2.832px, calc(100% - 10.610px) 4.024px, calc(100% - 11.976px) 5.390px, calc(100% - 13.168px) 6.911px, calc(100% - 14.167px) 8.564px, calc(100% - 14.960px) 10.326px, calc(100% - 15.535px) 12.171px, calc(100% - 15.883px) 14.071px, calc(100% - 16.000px) 16.000px, calc(100% - 16.000px) calc(100% - 35.000px), calc(100% - 16.255px) calc(100% - 30.781px), calc(100% - 17.017px) calc(100% - 26.624px), calc(100% - 18.274px) calc(100% - 22.589px), calc(100% - 20.009px) calc(100% - 18.735px), calc(100% - 22.196px) calc(100% - 15.118px), calc(100% - 24.802px) calc(100% - 11.791px), calc(100% - 27.791px) calc(100% - 8.802px), calc(100% - 31.118px) calc(100% - 6.196px), calc(100% - 34.735px) calc(100% - 4.009px), calc(100% - 38.589px) calc(100% - 2.274px), calc(100% - 42.624px) calc(100% - 1.017px), calc(100% - 46.781px) calc(100% - 0.255px), calc(100% - 51.000px) calc(100% - 0.000px), 51.000px calc(100% - 0.000px), 46.781px calc(100% - 0.255px), 42.624px calc(100% - 1.017px), 38.589px calc(100% - 2.274px), 34.735px calc(100% - 4.009px), 31.118px calc(100% - 6.196px), 27.791px calc(100% - 8.802px), 24.802px calc(100% - 11.791px), 22.196px calc(100% - 15.118px), 20.009px calc(100% - 18.735px), 18.274px calc(100% - 22.589px), 17.017px calc(100% - 26.624px), 16.255px calc(100% - 30.781px), 16.000px calc(100% - 35.000px), 16.000px 16.000px, 15.883px 14.071px, 15.535px 12.171px, 14.960px 10.326px, 14.167px 8.564px, 13.168px 6.911px, 11.976px 5.390px, 10.610px 4.024px, 9.089px 2.832px, 7.436px 1.833px, 5.674px 1.040px, 3.829px 0.465px, 1.929px 0.117px);--nav-notch-overhang:16px;--nav-notch-radius:35px;--nav-lens-blur:3px"><div class="nav-bar relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-6 pb-4"><div class="nav-shell"><svg class="nav-notch-shadow" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" preserveAspectRatio="none"><defs><filter id="nav-notch-shadow-blur" x="-50%" y="-50%" width="200%" height="200%"><feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="8.5"></feGaussianBlur></filter><mask id="nav-notch-shadow-mask" maskUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><rect data-field="true" fill="#fff"></rect><polygon data-cut="true" fill="#000"></polygon></mask></defs><g mask="url(#nav-notch-shadow-mask)"><polygon data-shape="true" fill="rgba(0, 58, 116, 0.16)" filter="url(#nav-notch-shadow-blur)" transform="translate(0 3)"></polygon></g></svg><div class="glass-filter"></div><div class="glass-overlay"></div><div class="nav-notch-sheen"></div><svg class="nav-notch-rim" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" preserveAspectRatio="none"><defs><linearGradient id="nav-notch-bevel" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#0b1a33" stop-opacity="0.13"></stop><stop offset="0.30" stop-color="#0b1a33" stop-opacity="0.03"></stop><stop offset="0.72" stop-color="#ffffff" stop-opacity="0.07"></stop><stop offset="1" stop-color="#ffffff" stop-opacity="0.40"></stop></linearGradient><linearGradient id="nav-notch-rim-gradient" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#8fa9c8" stop-opacity="0.10"></stop><stop offset="0.45" stop-color="#6e8cb2" stop-opacity="0.138"></stop><stop offset="0.78" stop-color="#4a6a9c" stop-opacity="0.213"></stop><stop offset="1" stop-color="